# Card hierarchy

Cards must have clear visual hierarchy — not uniform label/value grids that look like spreadsheets.

## Six content tiers

Use `CARD_CONTENT_TIERS` from `@oktavius/base-ui` — never ad-hoc font sizes inside cards.

| Tier | Use |
|---|---|
| 1 Hero | Record identity, primary metric |
| 2 Highlight | Important values with icon |
| 3 Body | Default field values |
| 4 Label | Field labels (sentence case) |
| 5 Meta | Subtitles, secondary context |
| 6 Micro | IDs, codes, audit footnotes |

Full reference: `docs/ui-rules/foundation.md` § Card content tiers.

## DetailView

```tsx
<DetailView
  title="Client record"
  fields={[
    { importance: 'primary', label: 'Email', value: client.email, icon: <EmailIcon size={20} weight="duotone" /> },
    { label: 'Industry', value: client.industry },
    { importance: 'meta', label: 'Client ID', value: client.id },
  ]}
/>
```

- **`primary`** — max 6 items, hero row with icons
- **`default`** — two-column grid
- **`meta`** — compact footer strip

## StatCard rows

```tsx
import { STAT_CARD_GRID_CLASS, StatCard } from '@oktavius/base-ui';

<div className={STAT_CARD_GRID_CLASS}>
  <StatCard label="Open cases" value="37" icon={<CaseIcon size={16} />} />
</div>
```

Max **6** StatCards per row. Fixed min-height for grid alignment.

## ListRow

- `title` — primary line (larger on `variant="queue"`)
- `subtitle` — secondary context
- `meta` — tertiary IDs/timestamps (mono micro tier)
- `visual` — shorthand for `RecordVisual` at `size="sm"` (logo, avatar, or icon)

## Record visuals

Use `RecordVisual` / `RecordIdentity` for the left-side anchor on cards and rows.

| Kind | Use |
|---|---|
| `image` | Logo or product photo when URL exists |
| `avatar` | Photo when `src` exists; otherwise required `icon` (people, orgs) |
| `icon` | Module/entity fallback when no photo |

```tsx
<RecordIdentity
  visual={{ kind: 'avatar', label: client.name, icon: <OrganizationIcon size={20} weight="duotone" /> }}
  title={client.name}
  subtitle={<StatusBadge … />}
/>
```
